  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Reflexive verbs use reflexive pronouns (me, te, se, nos) attached to the verb to indicate that the subject performs the action on itself, as in *afeitarse* ('to shave oneself'). \nClitic pronouns can sometimes convey possession, as in *Me limpiaba los dientes* ('I was cleaning my teeth'), where *me* indicates that the teeth belong to the subject.\nIn many contexts, Spanish uses simple past forms where English would use the present perfect."
    }
  ],
